==============================================================================
Intel Firmware Support Package (FSP) headers for the Kaby Lake FSP
  sys-boot/coreboot/files/3rdparty/fsp/KabylakeFspBinPkg/Include/

  https://github.com/intel/FSP/tree/master/KabylakeFspBinPkg
==============================================================================

coreboot takes the FSP UPD and HOB layouts from the headers of Intel's
Firmware Support Package.  Upstream coreboot gets them through its
3rdparty/fsp submodule, which the ChromiumOS checkout does not sync, so
sys-boot/coreboot carries the ten headers in its own files/ and copies them
into the coreboot source tree in the ebuild's src_prepare.  They come from
upstream chromiumos-overlay unchanged; WhaleOS added none of them:

  Include/FspUpd.h                        Copyright (c) 2019, Intel Corporation
  Include/FspmUpd.h                       Copyright (c) 2019, Intel Corporation
  Include/FspsUpd.h                       Copyright (c) 2019, Intel Corporation
  Include/FsptUpd.h                       Copyright (c) 2019, Intel Corporation
  Include/MemInfoHob.h                    Copyright (c) 1999 - 2018, Intel Corporation
  Include/GpioConfig.h                    Copyright (c) 2014 - 2016, Intel Corporation
  Include/GpioSampleDef.h                 Copyright (c) 2015, Intel Corporation
  Include/SmbiosCacheInfoHob.h            Copyright (c) 2015, Intel Corporation
  Include/SmbiosProcessorInfoHob.h        Copyright (c) 2015, Intel Corporation
  Include/ConfigBlock/CpuConfigFspData.h  Copyright (c) 2016, Intel Corporation

The files are included verbatim, with their original license headers.  No
FSP binary is part of the published overlay - neither the Kaby Lake Fsp.fd
itself nor the sample VBT that upstream ships beside these headers.

